          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Vicia lutea (yellow vetch, smooth yellow vetch) is a species of flowering plant in the bean family Fabaceae."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": " Distribution \nIt is native to Europe, western Asia, and North Africa, and it is known on other continents as an introduced species."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p4",
            "text": " Description \nIt is an annual herb. It has leaves made up of several pairs of oblong or linear leaflets each 1 to 2 centimeters long. It produces solitary flowers or clusters of up to 3 flowers with yellow or purple-tinged corollas up to 3 centimeters in length."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
